</style><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_astro/Shell.BG-gLcGo.css"></head><body id="page-top" class="utk destination-layout"><a href="#main" class="skip">Skip to content</a><div class="topline" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g><span data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>ROOTED IN ODISHA. OPEN TO THE WORLD.</span><span lang="or" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>ପ୍ରୋଜେକ୍ଟ ଓଡ଼ିଶା</span></div><header class="header wrap utk-header" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g><a class="home-link" href="/" aria-label="Project Odisha home" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g><span class="brand brand-en" lang="en"><img class="brand-signature" src="/assets/brand-v4/project-odisha-en-colour.svg" alt="Project Odisha" width="850" height="140"></span></a><nav class="utk-nav desktop-navigation" aria-label="Main navigation" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g><a href="/explore/" aria-current="page" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Explore</a><a href="/books/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Books</a><a href="/journey/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>My journey</a><a href="/about/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Our purpose</a><a class="nav-contribute utk-button utk-button--secondary" href="/contribute/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Be part of it <span aria-hidden="true" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>↗</span></a></nav><details class="mobile-navigation" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g><summary data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Menu</summary><nav aria-label="Main navigation" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g><a href="/explore/" aria-current="page" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Explore</a><a href="/books/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Books</a><a href="/journey/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>My journey</a><a href="/about/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Our purpose</a><a href="/contribute/" data-astro-cid-fzpbxy5g>Be part of it</a></nav></details></header><script type="module">var e=document.querySelector(`.mobile-navigation`);e?.addEventListener(`keydown`,t=>{t.key===`Escape`&&e.open&&(e.open=!1,e.querySelector(`summary`)?.focus(),t.preventDefault())});</script><main id="main" tabindex="-1"><article class="article-reading godabarish-article" data-astro-cid-udpgrjst><header data-astro-cid-udpgrjst><h1 data-astro-cid-udpgrjst>Godabarish Mahapatra and the Pages of Niankhunta</h1><p class="article-byline" data-astro-cid-6jw2r4la>By Ahimanikya Satapathy</p></header><p>Godabarish Mahapatra brought poetry and public criticism into the work of editing a periodical. Remembered as a poet and short-story writer, he was the founding editor of <em>Niankhunta</em>, an Odia magazine whose humour addressed public life.<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-1" id="user-content-fnref-1" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">1</a></sup><sup><a href="#user-content-fn-2" id="user-content-fnref-2" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">2</a></sup></p>
<figure data-astro-cid-udpgrjst><img src="/images/stories/godabarish-niankhunta.webp" alt="An illustrated open periodical, folded sheets and a fountain pen on a cream background." width="1200" height="800" class="astro-udpgrjst" srcset="/images/stories/godabarish-niankhunta-480.webp 480w, /images/stories/godabarish-niankhunta.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 740px) calc(100vw - 2.4rem), 696px" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-astro-cid-udpgrjst><figcaption data-astro-cid-udpgrjst>Editorial illustration of writing and a satirical periodical; not a reproduction of a Niankhunta issue. Illustration: Project Odisha.</figcaption></figure>
<h2 id="a-writer-and-a-recurring-public-voice">A writer and a recurring public voice</h2>
<p>Gouri Kumar Brahma’s account dates the start of <em>Niankhunta</em> to 1938 and describes Mahapatra’s use of wit to confront the conduct of socially powerful people. Brahma also draws attention to his sympathy for poorer people. Humour and concern for other lives belong together in this account of the writer: the joke can expose an abuse, while a story can give attention to the person living with its consequences.<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-2" id="user-content-fnref-2-2" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">2</a></sup></p>
<p>Mahapatra studied at Satyabadi Bana Bidyalaya. His mentor, Pandit Godabarish Mishra, was a different writer; their similar names should not merge their work. Brahma describes Mishra’s guidance in Mahapatra’s move to the school.<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-1" id="user-content-fnref-1-2" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">1</a></sup><sup><a href="#user-content-fn-2" id="user-content-fnref-2-3" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">2</a></sup></p>
<h2 id="what-a-magazine-page-can-tell-us">What a magazine page can tell us</h2>
<p>The first-volume scan places two-column political commentary and short verse among advertisements and publication notices. One imprint names D. M. Pattajosi as editor and a press at Berhampur; an adjacent notice records an editorial change. These details keep other participants visible. Mahapatra’s founding role does not establish his authorship of every unsigned passage.<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-3" id="user-content-fnref-3" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">3</a></sup></p>
<p>Read the imprint as carefully as the headline. Then follow the movement between prose and verse: where does the page slow the eye, and where does a shorter line interrupt it?</p>
<h2 id="poetry-beyond-the-periodical">Poetry beyond the periodical</h2>
<p>The Sahitya Akademi’s award register places <em>Banka O Sidha</em> in its 1966 Odia list, identifies it as poetry and marks the award to Godavarish Mahapatra as posthumous. Mahapatra had died on 25 November 1965. The award offers another entrance to his writing, alongside the magazine pages.<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-1" id="user-content-fnref-1-3" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">1</a></sup><sup><a href="#user-content-fn-4" id="user-content-fnref-4" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">4</a></sup></p>
<p>Odia Bibhaba’s chronological index credits most of its copies to Bhabani Shankar Mahapatra, the writer’s son and a former joint editor. Its holdings extend beyond the founder’s lifetime, with missing issues explicitly acknowledged. The surviving copies give readers a place to begin, without promising a complete run.<sup><a href="#user-content-fn-5" id="user-content-fnref-5" data-footnote-ref aria-describedby="footnote-label">5</a></sup></p>
<section data-footnotes class="article-footnotes"><h2 id="footnote-label">Footnotes &amp; Sources</h2>
<ol>
<li id="user-content-fn-1">
<p>Government of Odisha, <em>Orissa Reference Annual 2004</em>, “Eminent Literary Luminaries of Orissa,” <a href="https://magazines.odisha.gov.in/orissaannualreference/ORA-2004/pdf/eminent_literacy_luminaries_of_orissa.pdf">p. 297</a>, Godabarish Mohapatra entry. <a href="#user-content-fnref-1" data-footnote-backref="" aria-label="Back to reference 1" class="data-footnote-backref">↩</a> <a href="#user-content-fnref-1-2" data-footnote-backref="" aria-label="Back to reference 1-2" class="data-footnote-backref">↩<sup>2</sup></a> <a href="#user-content-fnref-1-3" data-footnote-backref="" aria-label="Back to reference 1-3" class="data-footnote-backref">↩<sup>3</sup></a></p>
</li>
<li id="user-content-fn-2">
<p>Gouri Kumar Brahma, <em>Godavarish Mahapatra</em>, <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1tPUCTFWvmaJrFKCiuDx5eKcrqDHm7qkG/view">English account linked by Odia Bibhaba</a>, printed pp. 2 and 4. <a href="#user-content-fnref-2" data-footnote-backref="" aria-label="Back to reference 2" class="data-footnote-backref">↩</a> <a href="#user-content-fnref-2-2" data-footnote-backref="" aria-label="Back to reference 2-2" class="data-footnote-backref">↩<sup>2</sup></a> <a href="#user-content-fnref-2-3" data-footnote-backref="" aria-label="Back to reference 2-3" class="data-footnote-backref">↩<sup>3</sup></a></p>
</li>
<li id="user-content-fn-3">
<p><em>Niankhunta</em>, <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1PwE1DA65NGjmbShAyHKVfOmErDy9hB19/view">volume 1 scan, catalogued 1938–39</a>, PDF pp. 6–8, digitised by Srujanika and linked by Odia Bibhaba. Selected pages, not a verified inaugural issue. <a href="#user-content-fnref-3" data-footnote-backref="" aria-label="Back to reference 3" class="data-footnote-backref">↩</a></p>
</li>
<li id="user-content-fn-4">
<p>Sahitya Akademi, <a href="https://sahitya-akademi.gov.in/awards/akademi%20samman_suchi.jsp">Akademi Awards</a>, Odia, 1966: <em>Banka O Sidha</em> (Poetry), Godavarish Mahapatra. The register’s asterisk denotes a posthumous award. <a href="#user-content-fnref-4" data-footnote-backref="" aria-label="Back to reference 4" class="data-footnote-backref">↩</a></p>
</li>
<li id="user-content-fn-5">
<p>Odia Bibhaba, <a href="https://odiabibhaba.in/en/magazines/niankhunta-e/">“Niankhunta” archive</a>, holdings index and donor acknowledgement. <a href="#user-content-fnref-5" data-footnote-backref="" aria-label="Back to reference 5" class="data-footnote-backref">↩</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>

